# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R1; the
# compiler-engineer's `dual`, in its other order).
#
# The case beside this one with its two groups swapped: `q` first, so `K`
# is 9 in both headers, and clang says nothing in this order either. The
# two programs differ only in the order of two groups and print different
# numbers, which is what spec § 4's *never matters but a group's* says.
extern "fixedbugs-563-q.h"
    function qk() -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-563-p.h"
    function pk() -> i32

function main()
    print(pk())
    print(qk())
